Third-party packages

The plugin does not bundle its dependencies in this repository. Paseo installs
them from npm with `npm ci` when the plugin is installed, and compiles them into
the server bundle on the host. Versions are pinned in package-lock.json.
License notes for packages with more than one license or with embedded code:

- imagescript: offered under AGPL-3.0-or-later OR MIT. This plugin uses it
  under the MIT License. Its THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md lists derived code.
- jszip (dependency of mammoth): offered under MIT OR GPL-3.0-or-later. This
  plugin uses it under the MIT License.
- libheif-js: LGPL-3.0. Used unmodified as published on npm, and replaceable
  through package.json and package-lock.json. Its WebAssembly build includes
  libheif (LGPL-3.0), libde265 (LGPL-3.0) and dav1d (BSD-2-Clause). Source:
  https://github.com/catdad-experiments/libheif-js
- @hyzyla/pdfium: MIT. Its WebAssembly build includes PDFium (BSD-3-Clause),
  FreeType (FreeType License), OpenJPEG (BSD-2-Clause), Anti-Grain Geometry
  and the other third-party code PDFium ships with. Source:
  https://pdfium.googlesource.com/pdfium/
- mammoth: BSD-2-Clause. heic-decode: ISC. utif2, pngjs: MIT. pako (dependency
  of jszip): MIT AND Zlib.
